#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:2
msgid "Porting from Distutils"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:4
msgid ""
"Setuptools and the PyPA have a `stated goal <https://github.com/pypa/"
"packaging-problems/issues/127>`_ to make Setuptools the reference API for "
"distutils."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:6
msgid ""
"Since the 60.0.0 release, Setuptools includes a local, vendored copy of "
"distutils (from late copies of CPython) that is enabled by default. To "
"disable the use of this copy of distutils when invoking setuptools, set the "
"environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:8
msgid "SETUPTOOLS_USE_DISTUTILS=stdlib"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:11
msgid ""
"Please note that this also affects how ``distutils.cfg`` files inside "
"stdlib's ``distutils`` package directory are processed. Unless "
"``SETUPTOOLS_USE_DISTUTILS=stdlib``, they will have no effect on the build "
"process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:15
msgid ""
"You can still use a global user config file, ``~/.pydistutils.cfg`` (POSIX) "
"or ``%USERPROFILE%/pydistutils.cfg`` (Windows), or use the environment "
"variable :ref:`DIST_EXTRA_CONFIG <setup-config>` to point to another "
"supplementary configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:21
msgid "Prefer Setuptools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:23
msgid ""
"As Distutils is deprecated, any usage of functions or objects from distutils "
"is similarly discouraged, and Setuptools aims to replace or deprecate all "
"such uses. This section describes the recommended replacements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:25
msgid "``distutils.core.setup`` → ``setuptools.setup``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:27
msgid ""
"``distutils.cmd.Command`` or ``distutils.core.Command`` → ``setuptools."
"Command``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:29
msgid ""
"``distutils.command.{build_clib,build_ext,build_py,sdist}`` → ``setuptools."
"command.*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:31
msgid "``distutils.dep_util`` → ``setuptools.modified``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:33
msgid "``distutils.log`` → :mod:`logging` (standard library)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:35
msgid ""
"``distutils.version.*`` → :doc:`packaging.version.* <packaging:version>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:37
msgid "``distutils.errors.*`` → ``setuptools.errors.*`` [#errors]_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:40
msgid ""
"Migration advice is also provided by :pep:`PEP 632 <632#migration-advice>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:42
msgid ""
"If a project relies on uses of ``distutils`` that do not have a suitable "
"replacement above, please search the `Setuptools issue tracker <https://"
"github.com/pypa/setuptools/issues/>`_ and file a request, describing the use-"
"case so that Setuptools' maintainers can investigate. Please provide enough "
"detail to help the maintainers understand how distutils is used, what value "
"it provides, and why that behavior should be supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deprecated/distutils-legacy.rst:45
msgid ""
"Please notice errors related to the command line usage of ``setup.py``, such "
"as ``DistutilsArgError``, are intentionally not exposed by setuptools, since "
"this is considered a deprecated practice."
msgstr ""
